[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why operators pick RTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
On [B]Paper 1.21[/B], measured on the in-repo benchmark harness, two clients spamming [I]/rtp[/I] back-to-back:

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Plugin[/TH][TH]TP/s[/TH][TH]Worst tick (MSPT p99)[/TH][TH]CPU per teleport[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]🧪 RTP[/B][/TD][TD][B]19.8[/B][/TD][TD][B]4 ms[/B][/TD][TD][B]16.9 ms[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 JakesRTP[/TD][TD]20.0[/TD][TD]70 ms[/TD][TD]26.0 ms[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 BetterRTP[/TD][TD]7.1[/TD][TD]771 ms[/TD][TD]53.6 ms[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 HuskHomes RTP[/TD][TD]6.2[/TD][TD]335 ms[/TD][TD]52.2 ms[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

Same throughput as the next-best plugin, [B]~17× lower worst-case tick spike, 35% less CPU per teleport.[/B] On Spigot, RTP's worst tick stays at 3 ms while competitors spike past 3 seconds. Reproduce on your own rig: [URL=https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3-beta/helpers/StressTestRTP][I]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/I][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#16A085]Install (30 seconds)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [I]RTP-x.y.z.jar[/I] into [I]plugins/[/I].
[*]Start the server. A [I]default[/I] region is generated for you.
[*]Type [B]/rtp[/B].
[/LIST]

That's it. Tune [I]plugins/RTP/config.yml[/I] and [I]plugins/RTP/regions/*.yml[/I] later. Full admin guide is auto-unpacked into [I]plugins/RTP/docs/[/I] on first run, and lives online at the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3-beta/docs/admin/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md'][B]admin guide[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#2980B9]What's in the box[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]🌀 [B]Deterministic spiral selection[/B] — bounded math, no unbounded re-roll loops. Predictable on huge worlds.
[*]🧠 [B]Spatial memory that persists across restarts[/B] — RTP [I]learns[/I] which sectors keep failing and stops trying them.
[*]⏱️ [B]Pre-generated location queue[/B] — most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve from a ready, chunk-loaded destination.
[*]🛡️ [B]Safety pipeline[/B] — radius check, invulnerability timer, optional landing platform, movement / damage cancel timers, material allow/deny list.
[*]🌍 [B]Per-region, per-world config[/B] — shapes (square / circle / rectangle), curve weighting, vertical adjustors, sky-light check, world overrides, hot-reloadable YAML.
[*]✨ [B]Effects on every lifecycle phase[/B] — particles, sounds, fireworks, potion, note effects via the in-tree [I]effects-api[/I], gated by [I]rtp.effects.<name>[/I] permissions.
[*]🔗 [B]Eight claim-plugin integrations bundled[/B] — GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect.
[*]🧩 [B]PlaceholderAPI, ProtocolLib, custom generators[/B] — Iris, Terra, datapacks work out of the box; modded biome IDs preserved.
[*]🛠️ [B]Public [I]rtp-api[/I][/B] — same surface as Pro. Trigger RTP from a GUI, NPC, or quest; build your own UX without forking.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

