[SPOILER='📚 Commands, placeholders, soft-deps']
[B]Commands[/B] (full reference: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3-beta/docs/admin/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md']admin guide[/URL])
[LIST]
[*][B]/rtp[/B] — teleport to the default region for your current world.
[*][B]/rtp [parameter]:[value][/B] — specify [I]region:[/I], [I]world:[/I], [I]player:[/I], or temporary overrides.
[*][B]/rtp reload[/B] — reload all configuration from disk.
[*][B]/rtp scan start|pause|resume|reset|cancel[/B] — pre-warm spatial memory by walking a region (renamed from [I]/rtp fill[/I] in 2.x).
[*][B]/rtp config[/B] — interactive config editor. [I]Experimental in 3.0.0-beta.1[/I]; edit YAML directly for production.
[/LIST]

[B]PlaceholderAPI[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]%rtp_player_status%[/B] — idle, waiting, teleporting, …
[*][B]%rtp_total_queue_length%[/B], [B]%rtp_public_queue_length%[/B], [B]%rtp_personal_queue_length%[/B]
[*][B]%rtp_teleport_world%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_x%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_y%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_z%[/B]
[/LIST]

[B]Soft dependencies (all optional):[/B] PlaceholderAPI, ProtocolLib. [I]PaperLib is no longer required. Vault economy ships in [B]RTP-Pro[/B].[/I]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='❓ FAQ']
[B]Q: Why is this so much faster than other RTP plugins?[/B]
A: Most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve from a pre-warmed queue — chunks are already loaded and safety-checked before you type the command. Two design choices make that queue cheap to keep full: a [B]persistent spatial memory[/B] per region (the plugin remembers which sectors of the world failed safety checks, so the spiral selector skips known-bad ground instead of rerolling forever), and an [B]off-tick async pre-filter[/B] (Anvil region files are read directly to reject unsafe biomes/blocks [I]before[/I] any chunk is loaded, so candidate verification never blocks the main thread). The pre-warmed queue is just the visible tip — the spatial memory keeps candidate selection bounded, and the async pre-filter keeps verification off the tick loop.

[B]Q: Does it work with Iris / Terra / custom datapack generators?[/B]
A: Yes. Region files are read directly, so modded and namespaced biome and block IDs are preserved. No configuration needed.

[B]Q: What's the difference between RTP and RTP-Pro?[/B]
A: Same engine, same source tree. [B]RTP-Pro[/B] adds the Folia adapter, multi-server / proxy support (beta.3+), SQL/Redis backends, Vault economy, multilingual [I]lang/**[/I], the richer block-tag/state-predicate [I]safety.yml[/I] grammar, and priority support. The free build is fully sufficient for single-server deployments. Drop in the Pro jar later — same config, same data, same commands.

[B]Q: I'm on Forge / NeoForge.[/B]
A: Run [B]Arclight[/B] or [B]Mohist[/B] (officially supported) and use this jar. A native Forge adapter is not planned.

[B]Q: Memory and MSPT — should I worry?[/B]
A: RTP trades a bounded amount of RAM (the queue, bounded by cacheCap) for speed. TPS should not drop below ~19 from RTP alone on a healthy server; MSPT spikes during new-area generation are expected — that's the cost of generating chunks, not RTP.

[B]Q: How do I report a bug?[/B]
A: GitHub issue with server version, RTP version, platform, relevant config files, and the error log section. See the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3-beta/docs/admin/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md']admin guide[/URL] for the full reproduction template.
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='🧪 Engineering receipts']
Every claim on this page is anchored in the repo:
[LIST]
[*][B]Reproducible benchmarks[/B] with raw artifacts: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3-beta/helpers/StressTestRTP'][B]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]Requirements traced to tests[/B] — every REQ-* (including the S-001…S-007 prohibition guards: no main-thread chunk loading, no silently swallowed teleport failures, …) has an implementing class and regression test: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3-beta/docs/dev/TRACEABILITY.md'][B]TRACEABILITY.md[/B][/URL]
[*][B]28+ ADRs[/B], dated and numbered, covering platform-in-scope decisions, the Anvil subsystem, the Brigadier bridge, supersession trails: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3-beta/docs/adr'][B]docs/adr/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]bStats[/B] enabled — anonymous usage stats help prioritize platform work.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='⚠️ Known limitations in 3.0.0-beta.2']
[LIST]
[*]Free build does not ship Folia, SQL/Redis, multi-server, Vault economy, multilingual [I]lang/**[/I], or the tag/state-predicate [I]safety.yml[/I] grammar — all are in [B]RTP-Pro[/B].
[*]Fabric is functional but an unstable frontier — usable, but expect rough edges; production-critical servers should prefer Paper/Folia/Spigot for now.
[*][I]safety.yml[/I] here accepts flat material names ([I]LAVA[/I], [I]MAGMA_BLOCK[/I], [I]CACTUS[/I], [I]FIRE[/I]). Unknown materials log one warning, never silently dropped.
[*][I]/rtp config[/I] is experimental; edit YAML directly for production.
[*]Edits to [I]safety.yml[/I] and biome filters do not yet invalidate the persisted shape cache — workaround: [I]/rtp scan reset <region>[/I].
[*]Emergency landing platform default is now [I]platformRadius: -1[/I] (disabled). Set to [I]0[/I] or higher to restore legacy 2.x behavior.
[/LIST]
Live list: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3-beta/CHANGELOG.md#known-issues']CHANGELOG[/URL].
[/SPOILER]

